  "user_id": 10,
  "reason": "KB-005 quick check: review recent sign-in attempts on disabled former-employee account for security escalation"
}

{
  "summary": "P1 security \u2013 reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, priya.nair@brightline.example): failed login alerts on former employee Ryan Brooks' account (ryan.brooks@brightline.example, user_id 10, Sales AE, left spring 2026). Findings (read-only): account status = disabled, but sign_in_blocked = false and vpn_access = TRUE (offboarding looks incomplete for VPN). Password last set 2026-03-23. Sign-in logs: 2 failed_password attempts on VPN, 2026-10-09 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 ET, overnight for the home time zone), from IP 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL, with no MFA. Looks like someone testing stolen or old credentials. No successful sign-ins in the 14-day window. Tier 1 took no action on this account: it's not the ticket sender's, and KB-005 says don't reset or unlock. Still needed: security review; consider block_sign_in and removing VPN access to finish offboarding; block or check IP 192.0.2.140; check whether the same IP hit other accounts; confirm the old credentials aren't reused anywhere else.",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate; P1 security; failed VPN attempts from a hosting network on a disabled account that still has VPN access"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for flagging this. Ryan's account is disabled, and we found 2 failed VPN sign-in attempts early this morning (around 3 AM Eastern) from a hosting network in Amsterdam. Both failed and nothing got in. One more thing: VPN access still shows as on for his account, so his offboarding may not be finished. I've escalated this to our Tier 2 security team as urgent. They'll review the attempts and decide next steps, like blocking sign-in completely and removing his VPN access. They'll follow up with you directly.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: Priya Nair (IT Manager, user 3, active). Target: Ryan Brooks (user 10, former Sales AE). Status is disabled, but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true. Sign-in logs: 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05 ET) from 192.0.2.140, hosting network, Amsterdam NL, no MFA. No successes. Under KB-005 I made no changes. The account isn't the sender's, so I didn't request block_sign_in, reset, or unlock. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1) recommending block_sign_in, removing VPN access, and reviewing the IP across other accounts.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
